                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "It\u2019s good practice to reference phosphor-dbus-interfaces (PDI) when describing association names, as it establishes context for why this change is needed.\n\nYou could reword the commit message like this for better clarity and flow:\n\n> Per [phosphor-dbus-interfaces](https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item.interface.yaml#L25), the relationship between PCIeSlot and PCIeDevices is modeled using the 'containing' / 'contained_by' association. bmcweb service relies on this documented association to generate the corresponding redfish links.\n>\n> In the current implementation, the slot-to-device relationship on Balcones systems was incorrectly modeled using a 'contains' to 'containing' association. This inconsistency breaks redfish functionality and affects redfish clients such as the WebGUI (PCIe Topology page)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
